    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Eight sets of fractures from brittle coating experiments were used to study the statistics of fracture sets at different development stages. Some parameters such as spatial density are more related to fluid flow capacities than other parameters. Fracture clustering is an important consideration in determining fracture development stages and fluid flow capacities. Together with other information, well bore fracture data can be used to predict subsurface fracture patterns, and estimate effective hydaulic conductivity.",
